course: dictionary
lesson: 12403
title: Curvature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Curvature is how much something curves or bends. A curve has curvature, and so does a bend in a road. «The road has a sharp curvature just before the bridge.» Here the word names the amount of bend.
explain: Curvature comes from curve. If you already know curve, you know most of this word. The ending turns it into a noun, which is a word for a thing, here the amount of bend.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The curvature of the Earth can be seen from a high plane.» The sentence is about the shape of the Earth, so curvature must be about how the Earth bends.
explain: Doctors use the word too. «The X-ray showed a curvature of Sam's spine.» Here the spine is the backbone, so curvature means it bends sideways or too much. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then check your meaning.
fact: Curvature means how much something curves or bends.
fact: «The curvature of the Earth» is what you can see from a high plane, which is evidence that the Earth is round.
fact: In maths, a small circle has more curvature than a big one, because it bends more sharply.
fact: «Curvature of the spine» means the backbone bends sideways or too much.
fact: Curve is the root word, so if you know curve, you can work out curvature.
exercise: «The curvature of the Earth can be seen from a high plane.» What does curvature mean here? | How bright the sun is | How far away the Moon is | *How much the Earth bends | How heavy the Earth is
exercise: Which has more curvature: a small circle or a big circle? | They have the same curvature | *The small circle | The big circle
exercise: Ella says curvature is a colour. What does it really mean? | A heavy weight | *How much something curves or bends | A bright shade of blue | A loud noise
test: «The X-ray showed a curvature of Sam's spine.» What does curvature mean in this sentence? | *The backbone bends sideways or too much | Sam has a sore knee | The X-ray was blurry | Sam's spine is very long
test: Which word is the root of curvature? | *curve | carve | cover
exam: Which sentence uses curvature correctly? | «My curvature is my favourite colour.» | *«The curvature of the road made the bus lean as it turned.» | «The curvature was bright and loud.» | «I ate a curvature for lunch.»
